IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gaq-common`

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Queensland) -- chapter 3 as a claimant meets it: whether an administrator
-- may be appointed for me (s 12), the advance appointment for a 17 1/2-year-old (s 13), who may be appointed (s 14,
-- with s 15(2), (3)), the court that approves my settlement or awards my damages (s 245, with s 239), the
-- administrator's notice to the registrar of titles (s 21(1), a regulative rule), when an appointment ends by itself
-- (s 26), review (ss 28, 29, 31), suspension (s 155) and what an administrator may do (s 33(2)).
--
-- SEAT: the adult whose capacity for a claim is in question. "The tribunal" is QCAT (sch 4). Every "is satisfied",
-- "considers" and "suspects" of the tribunal or a court is a fact asked of the person, answered conditionally.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Chapter 3: appointment of an administrator for my claim`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 12(1), (3) -- can the tribunal appoint an administrator for me?`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 12(1): "The tribunal may, by order, appoint a guardian for a personal matter, or an administrator for a financial
-- matter, for an adult if the tribunal is satisfied-- (a) the adult has impaired capacity for the matter; and (b) there
-- is a need for a decision in relation to the matter or the adult is likely to do something in relation to the matter
-- that involves, or is likely to involve, unreasonable risk to the adult's health, welfare or property; and (c) without
-- an appointment-- (i) the adult's needs will not be adequately met; or (ii) the adult's interests will not be
-- adequately protected." (3): "on its own initiative or on the application of the adult, the public guardian or an
-- interested person." An "if" condition: when a limb fails the tribunal has no power under s 12 (JUST FALSE in the
-- 2026-11-04 sense, given as the first limb that fails).
DECLARE `Can an administrator or guardian be appointed for me` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the tribunal may appoint one for the matter, on its own initiative or on your application, the public guardian's or an interested person's (s 12(1), (3))`
    `no: the tribunal is not satisfied you have impaired capacity for the matter (s 12(1)(a)); capacity is presumed until the contrary is proven (s 11(1))`
    `no: the tribunal is not satisfied there is a need for a decision, or an unreasonable risk to your health, welfare or property (s 12(1)(b))`
    `no: the tribunal is not satisfied that without an appointment your needs will not be adequately met or your interests will not be adequately protected (s 12(1)(c))`

GIVEN `the tribunal is satisfied I have impaired capacity for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal is satisfied there is a need for a decision or an unreasonable risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal is satisfied that without an appointment my needs or interests will not be adequately met or protected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can an administrator or guardian be appointed for me`
`s 12(1) -- appointment` `the tribunal is satisfied I have impaired capacity for the matter` `the tribunal is satisfied there is a need for a decision or an unreasonable risk` `the tribunal is satisfied that without an appointment my needs or interests will not be adequately met or protected` MEANS
    IF NOT `the tribunal is satisfied I have impaired capacity for the matter`
    THEN `no: the tribunal is not satisfied you have impaired capacity for the matter (s 12(1)(a)); capacity is presumed until the contrary is proven (s 11(1))`
    ELSE IF NOT `the tribunal is satisfied there is a need for a decision or an unreasonable risk`
         THEN `no: the tribunal is not satisfied there is a need for a decision, or an unreasonable risk to your health, welfare or property (s 12(1)(b))`
         ELSE IF NOT `the tribunal is satisfied that without an appointment my needs or interests will not be adequately met or protected`
              THEN `no: the tribunal is not satisfied that without an appointment your needs will not be adequately met or your interests will not be adequately protected (s 12(1)(c))`
              ELSE `yes: the tribunal may appoint one for the matter, on its own initiative or on your application, the public guardian's or an interested person's (s 12(1), (3))`

@export Can the tribunal (QCAT) appoint an administrator to run my claim and manage my money, or a guardian for a personal matter (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 12)?
GIVEN `the tribunal is satisfied I have impaired capacity for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the tribunal satisfied you have impaired capacity for the matter (for example running or settling your claim)?
      `the tribunal is satisfied there is a need for a decision or an unreasonable risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the tribunal satisfied a decision is needed about the matter, or that you are likely to do something about it that risks your health, welfare or property unreasonably?
      `the tribunal is satisfied that without an appointment my needs or interests will not be adequately met or protected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the tribunal satisfied that without an appointment your needs will not be adequately met, or your interests will not be adequately protected?
GIVETH A `Can an administrator or guardian be appointed for me`
DECIDE `Can an administrator be appointed for me question` IS
    `s 12(1) -- appointment` `the tribunal is satisfied I have impaired capacity for the matter` `the tribunal is satisfied there is a need for a decision or an unreasonable risk` `the tribunal is satisfied that without an appointment my needs or interests will not be adequately met or protected`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 13 -- the advance appointment for a young person about to turn 18`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 13(1): the tribunal may appoint a guardian or administrator "for an individual who is at least 17 1/2 years but not
-- 18 years" if satisfied of a reasonable likelihood of impaired capacity, need, and inadequacy "when the individual
-- turns 18". (3): "The appointment begins when the individual turns 18." (4): "The appointment ends when the individual
-- turns 19, unless the tribunal orders the appointment to be for a longer period." (5): the longer period only if the
-- tribunal considers the need will continue and the need for review is very limited. (6): "The longer period may be--
-- (a) if the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company ...--the period decided by the tribunal; or (b)
-- otherwise--a period of not more than 5 years." READINGS: 17 1/2 years is reached 210 months after birth (F4); the
-- "longer period" of s 13(6)(b) is the length of the whole appointment, counted from the 18th birthday, so it ends at
-- the latest on the 23rd birthday (fork F6: or 5 years more than the ordinary period, the 24th birthday). The (1)(a)-(c)
-- judgments are one fact, "the tribunal is satisfied of each likelihood".
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 13 -- the day I turn 17 1/2` `my date of birth` MEANS 210 `months after` `my date of birth`

GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 13(3) -- the day I turn 18` `my date of birth` MEANS 216 `months after` `my date of birth`

GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 13(4) -- the day I turn 19` `my date of birth` MEANS 228 `months after` `my date of birth`

GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 13(6)(b) -- the day I turn 23` `my date of birth` MEANS 276 `months after` `my date of birth`

DECLARE `Can an advance appointment be made for me` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are at least 17 1/2 but not 18; the appointment would begin when you turn 18 and end when you turn 19, unless the tribunal orders a longer period (s 13(1), (3), (4))`
    `no: you are not yet 17 1/2 (s 13(1))`
    `no: you are already 18; an ordinary appointment under s 12 is the route (s 13(1))`
    `no: the tribunal is not satisfied of each reasonable likelihood s 13(1)(a)-(c) requires`

GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `the tribunal is satisfied of each likelihood when I turn 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can an advance appointment be made for me`
`s 13(1) -- advance appointment` `my date of birth` `the day of the order` `the tribunal is satisfied of each likelihood when I turn 18` MEANS
    IF NOT ((`s 13 -- the day I turn 17 1/2` `my date of birth`) `is on or before` `the day of the order`)
    THEN `no: you are not yet 17 1/2 (s 13(1))`
    ELSE IF (`s 13(3) -- the day I turn 18` `my date of birth`) `is on or before` `the day of the order`
         THEN `no: you are already 18; an ordinary appointment under s 12 is the route (s 13(1))`
         ELSE IF `the tribunal is satisfied of each likelihood when I turn 18`
              THEN `yes: you are at least 17 1/2 but not 18; the appointment would begin when you turn 18 and end when you turn 19, unless the tribunal orders a longer period (s 13(1), (3), (4))`
              ELSE `no: the tribunal is not satisfied of each reasonable likelihood s 13(1)(a)-(c) requires`

@export I am nearly 18 and my injury claim may need managing. Can the tribunal make an advance appointment of an administrator or guardian for me now (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 13(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601)
      `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The date the tribunal would make the order (ISO 8601)
      `the tribunal is satisfied of each likelihood when I turn 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the tribunal satisfied that, when you turn 18, you are reasonably likely to have impaired capacity for the matter, to need a decision (or to risk your health, welfare or property), and to be left with needs unmet or interests unprotected without an appointment?
GIVETH A `Can an advance appointment be made for me`
DECIDE `Can an advance appointment be made for me question` IS
    `s 13(1) -- advance appointment` `my date of birth` `the day of the order` `the tribunal is satisfied of each likelihood when I turn 18`

-- What the latest end of an advance appointment is. NOTHING where the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee
-- company and the tribunal ordered a longer period: s 13(6)(a) leaves the period to the tribunal, with no cap.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the tribunal ordered a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 13(4)-(6) -- the latest end of the advance appointment` `my date of birth` `the tribunal ordered a longer period` `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the tribunal ordered a longer period`
    THEN JUST (`s 13(4) -- the day I turn 19` `my date of birth`)
    ELSE IF `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (`s 13(6)(b) -- the day I turn 23` `my date of birth`)

@export When does my advance appointment begin (s 13(3): when I turn 18)? Give my date of birth (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 13(3)).
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does my advance appointment begin question` IS
    `s 13(3) -- the day I turn 18` `my date of birth`

@export By when, at the latest, does my advance appointment end (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 13(4)-(6))? No answer means the tribunal decides the period, as it may for the public trustee or a trustee company.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601)
      `the tribunal ordered a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the tribunal order the appointment to last longer than until you turn 19?
      `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the administrator the public trustee or a trustee company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `When does my advance appointment end question` IS
    `s 13(4)-(6) -- the latest end of the advance appointment` `my date of birth` `the tribunal ordered a longer period` `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 14(1)(b), s 15(2), (3) -- who may be my administrator?`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 14(1): "The tribunal may appoint a person as guardian or administrator for a matter only if-- ... (b) for
-- appointment as an administrator, the person is-- (i) a person who is at least 18 years, not a paid carer, or health
-- provider, for the adult and not bankrupt or taking advantage of the laws of bankruptcy as a debtor under the
-- Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Cwlth) or a similar law of a foreign jurisdiction; or (ii) the public trustee or a trustee
-- company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968; and (c) having regard to the matters mentioned in section 15(1), the
-- tribunal considers the person appropriate for appointment." s 15(2), (3): being a relation of the adult, or a
-- possible beneficiary of the adult's estate, "does not, of itself," mean their interests are likely to conflict. An
-- "only if" list: outside it, JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `Kind of proposed administrator` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `the public trustee`
    `a trustee company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968`
    `another kind of body`

DECLARE `Can this person be my administrator` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the person is eligible and the tribunal considers them appropriate (s 14(1)(b), (c)); being your relative or a beneficiary of your estate does not of itself mean a conflict (s 15(2), (3))`
    `no: an individual administrator must be at least 18 (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
    `no: your paid carer or health provider cannot be your administrator (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
    `no: a bankrupt, or a person taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor, cannot be your administrator (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
    `no: only an individual, the public trustee or a trustee company may be an administrator (s 14(1)(b))`
    `no: the tribunal does not consider the person appropriate, having regard to the s 15(1) considerations (s 14(1)(c))`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of proposed administrator`
      `the person is at least 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is my paid carer or health provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is bankrupt or taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal considers the person appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can this person be my administrator`
`s 14(1) -- eligible administrator` `the kind` `the person is at least 18` `the person is my paid carer or health provider` `the person is bankrupt or taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor` `the tribunal considers the person appropriate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN
        IF NOT `the person is at least 18`
        THEN `no: an individual administrator must be at least 18 (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
        ELSE IF `the person is my paid carer or health provider`
             THEN `no: your paid carer or health provider cannot be your administrator (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
             ELSE IF `the person is bankrupt or taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor`
                  THEN `no: a bankrupt, or a person taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor, cannot be your administrator (s 14(1)(b)(i))`
                  ELSE `appropriate`
    WHEN `the public trustee` THEN `appropriate`
    WHEN `a trustee company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968` THEN `appropriate`
    WHEN `another kind of body` THEN `no: only an individual, the public trustee or a trustee company may be an administrator (s 14(1)(b))`
    WHERE
        `appropriate` MEANS
            IF `the tribunal considers the person appropriate`
            THEN `yes: the person is eligible and the tribunal considers them appropriate (s 14(1)(b), (c)); being your relative or a beneficiary of your estate does not of itself mean a conflict (s 15(2), (3))`
            ELSE `no: the tribunal does not consider the person appropriate, having regard to the s 15(1) considerations (s 14(1)(c))`

@export Can this person (a family member, a friend, the public trustee or a trustee company) be appointed as my administrator to manage my claim and money (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) ss 14(1), 15(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of proposed administrator` @desc Who is proposed: an individual; the public trustee; a trustee company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968; or another kind of body
      `the person is at least 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an individual: is the person at least 18?
      `the person is my paid carer or health provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an individual: is the person your paid carer (paid for your care other than by a government carer benefit or from damages for voluntary care) or your health provider?
      `the person is bankrupt or taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an individual: is the person bankrupt, or taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor (in Australia or abroad)?
      `the tribunal considers the person appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the tribunal consider the person appropriate, having regard to the general principles, any conflict of interest, compatibility with you, availability and competence?
GIVETH A `Can this person be my administrator`
DECIDE `Can this person be my administrator question` IS
    `s 14(1) -- eligible administrator` `the kind` `the person is at least 18` `the person is my paid carer or health provider` `the person is bankrupt or taking advantage of the bankruptcy laws as a debtor` `the tribunal considers the person appropriate`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 245 (with s 239) -- the court that approves my settlement or awards my damages`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 245(1): "This section applies if, in a civil proceeding-- (a) the court sanctions a settlement between another
-- person and an adult or orders an amount to be paid by another person to an adult; and (b) the court considers the
-- adult is a person with impaired capacity for a matter." (2): "The court may exercise all the powers of the tribunal
-- under chapter 3." (4): the registrar must, as soon as practicable, give a copy of the order to the tribunal. (7):
-- "court means the Supreme Court or the District Court. settlement includes compromise or acceptance of an amount paid
-- into court." s 239: the Act "does not affect rules of court ... about a litigation guardian". An "applies if"
-- condition: when it fails, s 245 gives the court no power (JUST FALSE); the tribunal's own power under s 12 remains.
DECLARE `Which court is my claim in` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court`
    `the District Court`
    `another court (for example the Magistrates Court)`

DECLARE `Can the court appoint my administrator` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court may itself appoint an administrator (or guardian) for you, with all the tribunal's chapter 3 powers, and must send the tribunal a copy of its order (s 245(2)-(4))`
    `no: s 245 applies only in the Supreme Court or the District Court (s 245(7)); the tribunal may still be asked under s 12`
    `no: s 245 applies only when the court sanctions a settlement (including a compromise or taking money paid into court) or orders money paid to you (s 245(1)(a)); the tribunal may still be asked under s 12`
    `no: s 245 applies only if the court considers you have impaired capacity for a matter (s 245(1)(b))`

GIVEN `the court` IS A `Which court is my claim in`
      `the court sanctions my settlement or orders money to be paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers I have impaired capacity for a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can the court appoint my administrator`
`s 245 -- settlements or damages awards` `the court` `the court sanctions my settlement or orders money to be paid to me` `the court considers I have impaired capacity for a matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court`
    WHEN `another court (for example the Magistrates Court)` THEN `no: s 245 applies only in the Supreme Court or the District Court (s 245(7)); the tribunal may still be asked under s 12`
    OTHERWISE
        IF NOT `the court sanctions my settlement or orders money to be paid to me`
        THEN `no: s 245 applies only when the court sanctions a settlement (including a compromise or taking money paid into court) or orders money paid to you (s 245(1)(a)); the tribunal may still be asked under s 12`
        ELSE IF NOT `the court considers I have impaired capacity for a matter`
             THEN `no: s 245 applies only if the court considers you have impaired capacity for a matter (s 245(1)(b))`
             ELSE `yes: the court may itself appoint an administrator (or guardian) for you, with all the tribunal's chapter 3 powers, and must send the tribunal a copy of its order (s 245(2)-(4))`

@export My injury claim is being settled or I am being awarded damages in court. Can that court appoint an administrator to manage the money for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 245)?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `Which court is my claim in` @desc Which court the civil proceeding is in: the Supreme Court; the District Court; or another court
      `the court sanctions my settlement or orders money to be paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court sanctioning a settlement (including a compromise, or accepting money paid into court) between you and another person, or ordering another person to pay you an amount?
      `the court considers I have impaired capacity for a matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider you have impaired capacity for a matter (for example managing the money)?
GIVETH A `Can the court appoint my administrator`
DECIDE `Can the court appoint my administrator question` IS
    `s 245 -- settlements or damages awards` `the court` `the court sanctions my settlement or orders money to be paid to me` `the court considers I have impaired capacity for a matter`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 21(1), s 31(5)(c) -- the administrator must tell the registrar of titles about land`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 21(1): "If the tribunal appoints an administrator for a matter involving an interest in land, the tribunal and the
-- administrator must each, within 3 months of the appointment, advise the registrar of titles." (3): the administrator
-- pays the titles registry fee. s 31(5)(c): an appointee is "no longer competent" if the appointee "fails to advise the
-- registrar of titles of the appointment as required under section 21(1)", a ground for removal at review. The
-- administrator's half is a regulative rule counted in days from the appointment; "within 3 months of" read as ending
-- on the same day number 3 months on (F1). The tribunal's own half is not encoded (an official's duty).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Guardianship party` `Guardianship act`
`s 21(1) -- the administrator advises the registrar of titles` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the administrator`
    MUST `advise the registrar of titles of the appointment`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the administrator` BECAUSE "s 21(1): the administrator did not advise the registrar of titles within 3 months of an appointment involving an interest in land; a ground for removal at review (s 31(5)(c))"

GIVEN `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(1) -- the last day to advise the registrar of titles` `the day of the appointment` MEANS 3 `months after` `the day of the appointment`

@export My administrator was appointed for a matter involving my land. By what day must the administrator advise the registrar of titles (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 21(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The date the tribunal appointed the administrator (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Last day to advise the registrar of titles question` IS
    `s 21(1) -- the last day to advise the registrar of titles` `the day of the appointment`

DECLARE `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(1) does not apply: the appointment does not involve an interest in land`
    `yes: your administrator advised the registrar of titles within 3 months of the appointment (s 21(1))`
    `no: your administrator advised the registrar of titles late; that is a ground for removal at review (s 31(5)(c))`
    `not yet due: the 3 months have not ended (s 21(1))`
    `overdue: the 3 months have ended and your administrator has not advised the registrar of titles; that is a ground for removal at review (s 31(5)(c))`

GIVEN `the appointment involves an interest in my land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the administrator has advised the registrar of titles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the administrator advised` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time`
`s 21(1) -- advice in time` `the appointment involves an interest in my land` `the day of the appointment` `the administrator has advised the registrar of titles` `the day the administrator advised` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT `the appointment involves an interest in my land`
    THEN `s 21(1) does not apply: the appointment does not involve an interest in land`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the state of` `advise the registrar of titles of the appointment` `by` `the administrator` `under` (`s 21(1) -- the administrator advises the registrar of titles` (`the number of days from` `the day of the appointment` `until` (`s 21(1) -- the last day to advise the registrar of titles` `the day of the appointment`))) `from` `the day of the appointment` `done` `the administrator has advised the registrar of titles` `on` `the day the administrator advised` `as at` `today`
         WHEN `yes: it was done within the period the Act allows` THEN `yes: your administrator advised the registrar of titles within 3 months of the appointment (s 21(1))`
         WHEN `no: it was done, but after the period the Act allows had ended` THEN `no: your administrator advised the registrar of titles late; that is a ground for removal at review (s 31(5)(c))`
         WHEN `not yet due: it has not been done, but the period has not ended` THEN `not yet due: the 3 months have not ended (s 21(1))`
         WHEN `overdue: the period the Act allows has ended and it has not been done` THEN `overdue: the 3 months have ended and your administrator has not advised the registrar of titles; that is a ground for removal at review (s 31(5)(c))`

@export Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles of the appointment in time (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) ss 21(1), 31(5)(c))?
GIVEN `the appointment involves an interest in my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the administrator appointed for a matter involving an interest in your land?
      `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The date the tribunal appointed the administrator (ISO 8601)
      `the administrator has advised the registrar of titles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the administrator advised the registrar of titles of the appointment?
      `the day the administrator advised` IS A DATE @desc The date the administrator advised the registrar of titles (ISO 8601); if not yet, any date
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time`
DECIDE `Has my administrator advised the registrar of titles in time question` IS
    `s 21(1) -- advice in time` `the appointment involves an interest in my land` `the day of the appointment` `the administrator has advised the registrar of titles` `the day the administrator advised` `today`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 26 -- when the appointment ends by itself`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 26(1): an appointment as guardian or administrator ends if "(a) the guardian or administrator becomes a paid carer,
-- or health provider, for the adult; or (b) ... becomes the service provider for a residential service where the adult is
-- a resident; or (c) if [they] and the adult are married when the appointment is made--the marriage is dissolved; or (d)
-- ... civil partnership ... terminated ...; or (e) the guardian or administrator dies; or (f) the adult dies". (2): an
-- administrator's appointment also ends if "(a) the administrator becomes bankrupt or insolvent". (3): after (1)(a)-(d),
-- (f) or (2) "the former guardian or administrator must advise the tribunal in writing". Limbs (1)(g) (restrictive
-- practices) and (2)(b) (missing persons) are out of scope. Read with "ends if" as a closed list for automatic ending
-- (s 26 heading "Automatic revocation"); other events end it only by withdrawal (s 27) or review (s 31).
DECLARE `What has happened` IS ONE OF
    `my administrator became my paid carer or health provider`
    `my administrator became the service provider of the residential service where I live`
    `my marriage to my administrator, in place when they were appointed, was dissolved`
    `my civil partnership with my administrator, in place when they were appointed, was terminated`
    `my administrator died`
    `my administrator became bankrupt or insolvent`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Has my administrator's appointment ended` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(1), (3))`
    `yes: the appointment has ended because your administrator died (s 26(1)(e))`
    `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(2)(a), (3))`
    `no: s 26 does not end the appointment on this event; it ends otherwise only on withdrawal with the tribunal's leave (s 27) or at a review (s 31)`

GIVEN `the event` IS A `What has happened`
GIVETH A `Has my administrator's appointment ended`
`s 26 -- automatic revocation` `the event` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `my administrator died` THEN `yes: the appointment has ended because your administrator died (s 26(1)(e))`
    WHEN `my administrator became bankrupt or insolvent` THEN `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(2)(a), (3))`
    WHEN `something else` THEN `no: s 26 does not end the appointment on this event; it ends otherwise only on withdrawal with the tribunal's leave (s 27) or at a review (s 31)`
    OTHERWISE `yes: the appointment has ended, and your former administrator must advise the tribunal in writing (s 26(1), (3))`

@export Something has changed for my administrator. Has the appointment ended by itself (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 26)?
GIVEN `the event` IS A `What has happened` @desc What happened: your administrator became your paid carer or health provider; became the service provider of your residential service; your marriage or civil partnership with them (in place at appointment) ended; they died; they became bankrupt or insolvent; or something else
GIVETH A `Has my administrator's appointment ended`
DECIDE `Has my administrator's appointment ended question` IS
    `s 26 -- automatic revocation` `the event`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 28, 29(1)(b) -- review of the appointment`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 28(1): "The tribunal must review an appointment of a guardian or administrator (other than the public trustee or a
-- trustee company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968)-- (a) for an appointment made because an adult has impaired
-- capacity for a matter but the tribunal does not consider the impaired capacity is permanent--in accordance with an
-- order of the tribunal, but at least every 5 years; or (b) otherwise--at least every 5 years." s 14(7): for a
-- non-permanent impaired capacity the order states when review is appropriate. READING: "at least every 5 years" runs
-- from the appointment or the last review; the next review is due by the earlier of that 5-year day and any day the
-- order sets (F1). For the public trustee or a trustee company, s 28 sets no periodic review: NOTHING (a scope limit,
-- "(other than ...)", fork F7); s 29 still lets you ask for one.
GIVEN `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the appointment or the last review` IS A DATE
      `the order sets an earlier review day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the review day the order sets` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 28(1) -- the next periodic review` `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company` `the day of the appointment or the last review` `the order sets an earlier review day` `the review day the order sets` MEANS
    IF `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the order sets an earlier review day`
         THEN JUST (`the earlier of` `the review day the order sets` `and` (60 `months after` `the day of the appointment or the last review`))
         ELSE JUST (60 `months after` `the day of the appointment or the last review`)

@export By when must the tribunal review my administrator's appointment (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 28)? No answer means s 28 sets no periodic review because the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company; you can still ask for a review under s 29.
GIVEN `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your administrator the public trustee or a trustee company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968?
      `the day of the appointment or the last review` IS A DATE @desc The date of the appointment, or of the tribunal's last review of it (ISO 8601)
      `the order sets an earlier review day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the tribunal's order (made because it did not consider your impaired capacity permanent) state when the appointment should be reviewed?
      `the review day the order sets` IS A DATE @desc The review date the order states (ISO 8601); if none, any date
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By when must my appointment be reviewed question` IS
    `s 28(1) -- the next periodic review` `the administrator is the public trustee or a trustee company` `the day of the appointment or the last review` `the order sets an earlier review day` `the review day the order sets`

-- s 29(1): "The tribunal may review an appointment of a guardian or administrator for an adult at any time-- (a) on its
-- own initiative; or (b) for a guardian (other than ... restrictive practice ...) or an administrator--on the
-- application of any of the following-- (i) the adult; (ii) an interested person for the adult; (iii) the public trustee;
-- (iv) a trustee company under the Trustee Companies Act 1968". A closed list of applicants.
DECLARE `Who wants the review` IS ONE OF
    `the adult (me)`
    `an interested person for the adult`
    `the public trustee or a trustee company`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `who applies` IS A `Who wants the review`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(1)(b) -- may apply for a review` `who applies` IF
    CONSIDER `who applies`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Can I (or someone with a genuine concern for me) ask the tribunal to review my administrator's appointment at any time (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 29(1)(b))?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A `Who wants the review` @desc Who would apply: you (the adult); an interested person (someone with a sufficient and genuine concern for your rights and interests); the public trustee or a trustee company; or someone else
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask for a review of the appointment question` IS
    `s 29(1)(b) -- may apply for a review` `who applies`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 31(2)-(5) -- what the review can do`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 31(2): "At the end of the review, the tribunal must revoke its order making the appointment unless it is satisfied
-- it would make an appointment if a new application for an appointment were to be made." (3): if satisfied, it may
-- continue or change the order. (4): "However, the tribunal may make an order removing an appointee, other than the
-- public guardian, only if the tribunal considers-- (a) the appointee is no longer competent; or (b) another person is
-- more appropriate for appointment." (5): no longer competent "if, for example-- (a) a relevant interest of the adult has
-- not been ... adequately protected; or (b) the appointee has neglected the appointee's duties or abused the appointee's
-- powers ...; or (c) ... fails to advise the registrar of titles ... under section 21(1); or (d) the appointee has
-- otherwise contravened this Act." The (5) examples are folded into the one fact "the tribunal considers the
-- administrator no longer competent". The public guardian is a guardian, not an administrator: not modelled.
DECLARE `What can the review do to my administrator's appointment` IS ONE OF
    `the appointment must be revoked: the tribunal is not satisfied it would appoint on a new application (s 31(2))`
    `the tribunal may continue or change the order, and may remove your administrator (s 31(3), (4))`
    `the tribunal may continue or change the order, but may not remove your administrator: it does not consider them no longer competent or another person more appropriate (s 31(3), (4))`

GIVEN `the tribunal is satisfied it would appoint on a new application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal considers my administrator no longer competent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal considers another person more appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What can the review do to my administrator's appointment`
`s 31 -- the review outcome` `the tribunal is satisfied it would appoint on a new application` `the tribunal considers my administrator no longer competent` `the tribunal considers another person more appropriate` MEANS
    IF NOT `the tribunal is satisfied it would appoint on a new application`
    THEN `the appointment must be revoked: the tribunal is not satisfied it would appoint on a new application (s 31(2))`
    ELSE IF `the tribunal considers my administrator no longer competent` OR `the tribunal considers another person more appropriate`
         THEN `the tribunal may continue or change the order, and may remove your administrator (s 31(3), (4))`
         ELSE `the tribunal may continue or change the order, but may not remove your administrator: it does not consider them no longer competent or another person more appropriate (s 31(3), (4))`

@export What can a review do to my administrator's appointment: must it be revoked, and can my administrator be removed (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 31(2)-(5))?
GIVEN `the tribunal is satisfied it would appoint on a new application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the tribunal satisfied it would appoint an administrator for you if a new application were made now?
      `the tribunal considers my administrator no longer competent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the tribunal consider your administrator no longer competent (for example your interests were not adequately protected, they neglected their duties or abused their powers, did not advise the registrar of titles as s 21(1) requires, or otherwise contravened the Act)?
      `the tribunal considers another person more appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the tribunal consider another person more appropriate to be your administrator?
GIVETH A `What can the review do to my administrator's appointment`
DECIDE `What can the review do question` IS
    `s 31 -- the review outcome` `the tribunal is satisfied it would appoint on a new application` `the tribunal considers my administrator no longer competent` `the tribunal considers another person more appropriate`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 155 -- suspension of my administrator`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 155(1): the tribunal "may, by order, suspend the operation of all or some of the power of a guardian or administrator
-- ... if the tribunal suspects, on reasonable grounds, that the appointed person is not competent." (4): "The suspension
-- may not be for more than 3 months." (6): "During the suspension of the operation of power of an administrator, the
-- public trustee is taken to be the administrator for the adult for the exercise of the suspended power." READING: a
-- suspension from a day may run to the same day number 3 months on, at the latest (F1).
GIVEN `the day the suspension starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 155(4) -- the latest end of the suspension` `the day the suspension starts` MEANS 3 `months after` `the day the suspension starts`

@export The tribunal has suspended my administrator's power because it suspects they are not competent. Until when, at the latest, can the suspension last (the public trustee acts meanwhile) (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 155(4), (6))?
GIVEN `the day the suspension starts` IS A DATE @desc The date the suspension began (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Latest end of my administrator's suspension question` IS
    `s 155(4) -- the latest end of the suspension` `the day the suspension starts`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 33(2) -- can my administrator run and settle my claim?`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 33(2): "Unless the tribunal orders otherwise, an administrator is authorised to do, in accordance with the terms of
-- the administrator's appointment, anything in relation to a financial matter that the adult could have done if the
-- adult had capacity for the matter when the power is exercised." Sch 2 s 18(d): a legal matter includes "bringing or
-- defending a proceeding, including settling a claim". So an administrator appointed for the financial matter of my
-- claim may bring, run and settle it, unless the tribunal's order or the appointment's terms say otherwise. A court's
-- sanction of a settlement (rules of court, s 239) is outside this Act and not encoded.
DECLARE `Can my administrator run and settle my claim` IS ONE OF
    `yes: your administrator may bring, run and settle the claim as you could if you had capacity (s 33(2), sch 2 s 18(d))`
    `no: the claim is not a financial matter, so it is for a guardian, not your administrator (s 33(2), sch 2 s 2(i))`
    `no: your administrator's appointment does not cover the claim, or the tribunal has ordered otherwise (s 33(2))`

GIVEN `the claim relates to my money or property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment covers the claim and no tribunal order says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can my administrator run and settle my claim`
`s 33(2) -- the administrator's power over my claim` `the claim relates to my money or property` `the appointment covers the claim and no tribunal order says otherwise` MEANS
    IF NOT `the claim relates to my money or property`
    THEN `no: the claim is not a financial matter, so it is for a guardian, not your administrator (s 33(2), sch 2 s 2(i))`
    ELSE IF `the appointment covers the claim and no tribunal order says otherwise`
         THEN `yes: your administrator may bring, run and settle the claim as you could if you had capacity (s 33(2), sch 2 s 18(d))`
         ELSE `no: your administrator's appointment does not cover the claim, or the tribunal has ordered otherwise (s 33(2))`

@export Can my administrator bring, run and settle my compensation claim for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2000 (Qld) s 33(2), sch 2 s 18)?
GIVEN `the claim relates to my money or property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claim relate to your money or property (for example damages or compensation payable to you)?
      `the appointment covers the claim and no tribunal order says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms of your administrator's appointment cover the claim (or all financial matters), with no tribunal order limiting it?
GIVETH A `Can my administrator run and settle my claim`
DECIDE `Can my administrator settle my claim question` IS
    `s 33(2) -- the administrator's power over my claim` `the claim relates to my money or property` `the appointment covers the claim and no tribunal order says otherwise`
